<title>UK: Bass shares drop after trading statement.</title>
<headline>Bass shares drop after trading statement.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>- Shares in brewing-to-hotels group Bass Plc dropped on Thursday, after the company issued a cautious trading statement at its annual meeting.</p>
<p>The stock was down 21-1/2p at 831p by 1221 GMT, after dropping as much as 26-1/2p in the wake of the AGM statement. Prior to that the stock had been up 8-1/2p.  </p>
<p>Bass said it had continued to make progress in the first 16 weeks of the year but trading was running slightly below its earlier expectations.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
